                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "It feels inconsistent when you've chosen 'static' and when you haven't.  I only bring it up because I would have expected it to be more useful in a header file to be 'static' or 'inline' than in a function, like here, but you've seemingly chose the opposite of my intuition."
                },
                {
                    "file": "platform-mc/test/event_manager_test.cpp",
                    "line": 44,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "I think most of the headers already had unqualified constexpr in them so I just followed the pattern.  If it makes sense I will do a follow up patch that changes them all to inline? (I think tidy has a rule for that too?)\n\nIn this file, I am probably used to pre-constexpr static const to get symbols into rodata vs just const which I think gets them pushed/popped from the stack.  I take it unqualified constexpr is idiomatic for this case?"
                },
                {
